description:
Implement a small inventory on top of `std::map<std::string, int>`. Every member's page states what happens when the item already exists or is missing; the map member functions in lesson 2.02 differ in exactly those cases, so pick each one to match.

```cpp-norun
class Inventory
{
public:
    bool addNew(const std::string& item, int count);
    bool set(const std::string& item, int count);
    int countOf(const std::string& item) const;
    bool take(const std::string& item, int n);
    std::size_t removeEmpty();
    std::size_t size() const;
    std::vector<std::string> items() const;
};
```

- **addNew**: adds the item with `count` only if it is not there yet. Returns true if it was added. An existing item's count is **not** changed.
- **set**: sets the item's count, adding the item if it is missing. Returns true if the item was **new**.
- **countOf**: the item's count, or 0 if it is missing. Never adds an item.
- **take**: if the item exists and has at least `n`, subtracts `n` and returns true. Otherwise returns false and changes nothing. An item that reaches 0 stays in the inventory.
- **removeEmpty**: removes every item whose count is 0 and returns how many were removed.
- **size**: the number of items. **items**: their names in sorted order.

